Subject: [DXMT] dxgi: return an explicit error for unimplemented teardown notifications

Source: gauthierpiarrette/dxmt 7421db2076b7e4ef36be167294023feefbe7ba7e.
The old assert-only HRESULT function falls through under NDEBUG. Do not report
successful registration, create a cookie, signal or take ownership of an event.
The matching void unregister operation has no registration to release.

Contract: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/dxgi1_4/nf-dxgi1_4-idxgiadapter3-registerhardwarecontentprotectionteardownstatusevent
An unsuccessful registration returns an HRESULT error; E_NOTIMPL describes
this backend's current implementation, not an observed native Windows result.

--- a/src/dxgi/dxgi_adapter.cpp
+++ b/src/dxgi/dxgi_adapter.cpp
@@ -225,12 +225,13 @@
   HRESULT STDMETHODCALLTYPE
   RegisterHardwareContentProtectionTeardownStatusEvent(HANDLE event,
                                                        DWORD *cookie) override {
-    assert(0 && "TODO");
+    Logger::err("DXGI: hardware content protection teardown notification is not implemented");
+    return E_NOTIMPL;
   }
 
   void STDMETHODCALLTYPE
   UnregisterHardwareContentProtectionTeardownStatus(DWORD cookie) override {
-    assert(0 && "TODO");
+    Logger::err("DXGI: no hardware content protection teardown notification was registered");
   }
 
   HRESULT STDMETHODCALLTYPE QueryVideoMemoryInfo(
